                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 55.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 242.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            29, 1870</date>. (Received August 11, 1870.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have just learned, what may be a matter
                    of some interest to you, that the subjects of Bavaria, Würtemberg, and Baden
                    have been put under the protection of the Swiss minister, Mr. Kern, during the
                    war between France and Prussia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
